### Problem description & steps to reproduce

(This was found with assistance by Claude Opus 5; I reviewed and validated the bug)

When you rollback >1 tokens, the KV cache slots for tokens are not cleared (just masked away with -Inf before softmax). This *should* have no effect because exp(-inf + x) = +0 for any finite x, the stale slot's attention score. So, as long as V is finite (otherwise `0*Inf = NaN`), IEEE 754-2019 §7.2, §6.3 suggests the attention sum would be unchanged (`+0*V = +/- 0`; no effect if the computations are IEEE conformant). As the code shows below, however, the masked-out slots do have a (very small; unless V is ever Inf in which case it is a large effect... corrupting a sum) effect.

This bug does NOT occur if either `GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT=1` or the computation is done on the CPU. This suggests a shader issue. I believe, specifically, it is [this shader](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/4cb22cd537a9b12b717bd725b3fecb83c94894eb/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_cm1.comp#L479-L496) lines 479-496 specifically `PVMat = coopMatMulAdd(KMat, QMat, PVMat);`. This can be fixed by zeroing fully-masked K/V columns while staging the tile.

This looks like one of the mechanisms behind [#25618](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25618). It is independent of the GQA-packing problem being fixed in [#26358](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/26358).

(The following test script was originally written under my direction by Claude Opus 5, but I read/understood each line and modified it for brevity and clarity)

```
// build from the llama.cpp root, after cmake --build build:
// g++ -O2 -std=c++17 fa_stale_kv_leak.cpp -o build/bin/fa_stale_kv_leak -Iinclude -Iggml/include \
//     -Lbuild/bin -lllama -lggml -lggml-base -Wl,-rpath,'$ORIGIN'
// the binary must land in build/bin: backends load from the executable's own directory

#include "llama.h"
#include "ggml-backend.h"
#include <cstdio>
#include <vector>

static const int WARM = 12, N = 2;   // history; block to decode-then-remove (1 freed cell keeps its K/V)
static llama_model * model;
static int nvoc;

static void feed(llama_context * c, int pos, int n) {
    llama_batch b = llama_batch_init(n, 0, 1);
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        b.token[i] = (1000 + pos + i) % nvoc; b.pos[i] = pos + i;
        b.n_seq_id[i] = 1; b.seq_id[i][0] = 0; b.logits[i] = 1;
    }
    b.n_tokens = n;
    llama_decode(c, b);
    llama_batch_free(b);
}

// logits for the token after position WARM, optionally decoding a block there first and
// removing it again -- which must not change anything
static std::vector<float> predict(bool stale, bool fa) {
    llama_context_params cp = llama_context_default_params();
    cp.n_ctx = 256; cp.n_batch = WARM + N + 1;
    cp.flash_attn_type = fa ? LLAMA_FLASH_ATTN_TYPE_ENABLED : LLAMA_FLASH_ATTN_TYPE_DISABLED;
    llama_context * c = llama_init_from_model(model, cp);

    for (int i = 0; i < WARM; i++) feed(c, i, 1);
    if (stale) {
        feed(c, WARM, N);
        llama_memory_seq_rm(llama_get_memory(c), 0, WARM, -1);
    }
    feed(c, WARM, 1);

    const float * lg = llama_get_logits_ith(c, -1);
    std::vector<float> out(lg, lg + nvoc);
    llama_free(c);
    return out;
}

int main(int argc, char ** argv) {
    if (argc != 2) { fprintf(stderr, "usage: %s model.gguf\n", argv[0]); return 2; }
    ggml_backend_load_all();
    llama_backend_init();
    llama_model_params mp = llama_model_default_params();
    mp.n_gpu_layers = 99;
    model = llama_model_load_from_file(argv[1], mp);
    if (!model) return 2;
    if (llama_model_is_recurrent(model) || llama_model_is_hybrid(model)) {
        // rollback on recurrent models is separately broken (#26695) and would confound
        // this test; use a plain transformer
        fprintf(stderr, "needs a non-recurrent model\n"); return 2;
    }
    nvoc = llama_vocab_n_tokens(llama_model_get_vocab(model));

    const bool fa_leaks = predict(false, true)  != predict(true, true);
    const bool no_leaks = predict(false, false) != predict(true, false);

    printf("FA on : %s\nFA off: %s\n%s\n",
           fa_leaks ? "logits CHANGED" : "logits identical",
           no_leaks ? "logits CHANGED" : "logits identical",
           fa_leaks ? "LEAK - freed cells influence the output" : "ok");
    llama_model_free(model);
    llama_backend_free();
    return fa_leaks;
}
